WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Journal club tomorrow. Your figures still look blurry.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.800
You’ve read every figure. What story will you tell?

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.100
Select a panel. Save it straight from the original PDF.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:18.600
Add your speaking note. Export a slide with the figure and its source.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:24.200
New to this plot? Start with what each point represents.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.400
Look for neighbours. Select an abbreviation for the paper’s own definition.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.300
Over what period were these cells sampled? Ask beside the figure.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.100
Day zero to four months. Open the caption on page ten.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.300
Preparing your talk? Open the paper map. Start with the authors’ question.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.800
Follow a branch to see what evidence a figure brings to that question.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.200
Go back to the figure. Pick the panel your audience needs.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.000
Try Reading Desk with the next paper you’re presenting.
